:"Luz","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H8481","lemma":"תַּחְתּוֹן","tr":"tach·ton","gloss":"Lower (Beth Horon)","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":17,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then the sons of Joseph said to Joshua, “Why have you given us only one portion as an inheritance? We have many people, because the LORD has blessed us abundantly.”","from":4},{"book":"JOS","chapter":18,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"On the north side their border began at the Jordan, went up past the northern slope of Jericho, headed west through the hill country, and came out at the wilderness of Beth-aven.","from":1},{"book":"JOS","chapter":18,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"From there the border crossed over to the southern slope of Luz (that is, Bethel) and went down to Ataroth-addar on the hill south of Lower Beth-horon.","from":2},{"book":"GEN","chapter":28,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and he called that place Bethel, though previously the city had been named Luz.","from":2},{"book":"NUM","chapter":34,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Your western border will be the coastline of the Great Sea; this will be your boundary on the west.","from":3},{"book":"JOS","chapter":8,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Joshua and all Israel let themselves be beaten back before them, and they fled toward the wilderness.","from":1},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":61,"verseEnd":61,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"These were in the wilderness: Beth-arabah, Middin, Secacah,","from":1},{"book":"JOS","chapter":18,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"From there the border crossed over to the southern slope of Luz (that is, Bethel) and went down to Ataroth-addar on the hill south of Lower Beth-horon.","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"5-10":{"people":[{"id":"ephraim-h0669g","name":"Ephraim","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":4,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"manasseh-h4519g","name":"Manasseh","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":9}],"places":[{"id":"ataroth-addar-h5853","name":"Ataroth-addar","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"beth-horon-upper-h1032h","name":"Beth-horon Upper","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"janoah-h3239b","name":"Janoah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"michmethath-h4366","name":"Michmethath","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"taanath-shiloh-h8387","name":"Taanath-shiloh","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"ataroth-h5852h","name":"Ataroth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"jericho-h3405g","name":"Jericho","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"jordan-h3383","name":"Jordan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"naaran-h5295","name":"Naaran","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"kanah-h7071g","name":"Kanah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"tappuah-h8599b","name":"Tappuah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"canaan-h3667a","name":"Canaan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"gezer-h1507","name":"Gezer","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10}],"words":[{"base":"H1366","lemma":"גְּבוּל","tr":"ge·vul","gloss":"border: boundary","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":240},{"base":"H0669","lemma":"אֶפְרַ֫יִם","tr":"eph·ra·yim","gloss":"Ephraim","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":180},{"base":"H8387","lemma":"תַּאֲנַת שִׁלֹ֑ה","tr":"ta·a·nat shi·loh","gloss":"Taanath-shiloh","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H4217","lemma":"מִזְרָח","tr":"miz·rach","gloss":"East (Gate)","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":74},{"base":"H3239","lemma":"יָנוֹחַ","tr":"ya·no·ach","gloss":"Janoah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":3},{"base":"H5853","lemma":"עַטְרוֹת אַדָּר","tr":"at·rot ad·dar","gloss":"Ataroth-addar","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H5159","lemma":"נַחֲלָה","tr":"na·cha·lah","gloss":"inheritance","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":222},{"base":"H1032","lemma":"בֵּית חוֹרֹן","tr":"bet cho·ron","gloss":"Beth-horon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":28},{"base":"H3220","lemma":"יָם","tr":"yam","gloss":"sea","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":396},{"base":"H3669","lemma":"כְּנַעֲנִי","tr":"ke·na·a·ni","gloss":"Canaanite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":73}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JDG","chapter":1,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Ephraim also failed to drive out the Canaanites living in Gezer; so the Canaanites continued to dwell among them in Gezer.","from":10},{"book":"DEU","chapter":7,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"When the LORD your God brings you into the land that you are entering to possess, and He drives out before you many nations—the Hittites, Girgashites, Amorites, Canaanites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites, seven nations larger and stronger than you—","from":10},{"book":"DEU","chapter":7,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"and when the LORD your God has delivered them over to you to defeat them, then you must devote them to complete destruction. Make no treaty with them and show them no mercy.","from":10},{"book":"JOS","chapter":17,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now the border of Manasseh went from Asher to Michmethath near Shechem, then southward to include the inhabitants of En-tappuah.","from":6},{"book":"JOS","chapter":18,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"From there the border crossed over to the southern slope of Luz (that is, Bethel) and went down to Ataroth-addar on the hill south of Lower Beth-horon.","from":5},{"book":"1KI","chapter":9,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Pharaoh king of Egypt had attacked and captured Gezer. He had set it on fire, killed the Canaanites who lived in the city, and given it as a dowry to his daughter, Solomonʼs wife.","from":10},{"book":"1CH","chapter":7,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Their holdings and settlements included Bethel and its villages, Naaran to the east, Gezer and its villages to the west, and Shechem and its villages as far as Ayyah and its villages.","from":7},{"book":"NUM","chapter":33,"verse":48,"verseEnd":48,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They set out from the mountains of Abarim and camped on the plains of Moab by the Jordan across from Jericho.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}